# SafeChat API Endpoints

## Quick reference

- **Base URL:** `https://<your-backend>/api/v1`
- **Local base URL:** `http://localhost:8000/api/v1`
- **JSON:** Send `Content-Type: application/json` for JSON request bodies.
- **Authentication:** Feature endpoints require `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>` unless marked **Public**. Root, health, and docs endpoints are public.
- **Success format:** Most endpoints return `{"success": true, "message": "...", "data": ...}`.
- **Application error format:** `{"success": false, "message": "...", "error_code": "...", "details": ...}`.
- **Admin access:** `/admin/*` requires an admin account. Endpoints marked **Superadmin** require the superadmin role.
- **API explorer:** `/docs` (Swagger), `/redoc`, and `/openapi.json` are outside the `/api/v1` prefix.

`{value}` in a path is a URL parameter. `?name=value` is a query parameter. Unless noted, inputs described below are JSON bodies.

## Service health

| Method and path | What it does | Input -> response |
|---|---|---|
| `GET /` | Identifies the service and links to docs and health. | None -> `name`, `version`, `docs`, `health`. |
| `GET /health` | Checks that the API process responds. | None -> `status`, `service`, `version`. |
| `GET /health/live` | Liveness probe for the API process. | None -> `status`. |
| `GET /health/ready` | Checks API readiness and MongoDB connectivity. | None -> `status`, `mongodb`; returns HTTP 503 when not ready. |

## Authentication

| Method and path | What it does | Input -> response |
|---|---|---|
| `GET /auth/username/check` | Checks whether a username is available. **Public** | Query `username` -> `available` and, when relevant, `reason`. |
| `GET /auth/phone/check` | Checks whether a phone number is available. **Public** | Query `phone` -> `available` and, when relevant, `reason`. |
| `POST /auth/phone/send-code` | Starts phone verification. **Public; development stub** | `{phone_number}` or `{phone}` -> normalized number, `sent: true`, and `dev_code: "000000"`. |
| `POST /auth/phone/verify-code` | Verifies the phone code. **Public; development stub** | `{phone_number, code}` (or `phone`; code must be at least 4 characters) -> `verified`, `registration_token`. |
| `POST /auth/register` | Creates an account. **Public** | `{username, display_name, password, email?, phone_number?, profile_photo?, bio?}` -> `user` (HTTP 201). |
| `POST /auth/login` | Signs in with username or phone. **Public** | `{username? or phone_number?, password, device_id?, device_name?}` -> user and access/refresh tokens. The refresh token is also set as an HttpOnly cookie. |
| `POST /auth/password-reset/request` | Emails a temporary reset credential when the account exists. **Public** | `{email}` -> generic confirmation message (does not reveal whether the account exists). |
| `POST /auth/password-reset/complete` | Sets a new password with a reset credential. **Public** | `{reset_login_token, new_password}` -> `revoked_sessions`. |
| `POST /auth/refresh` | Renews the access token. **Public** | `{refresh_token?}` or the `sc_refresh` cookie -> new access token and the same refresh token. |
| `POST /auth/logout` | Ends the refresh-token session. **Public** | `{refresh_token?}` or the `sc_refresh` cookie -> confirmation; clears the cookie. |
| `GET /auth/me` | Returns the signed-in user and current account settings. | None -> user profile, role, plan, preferences, and premium settings. |
| `POST /auth/change-password` | Changes the signed-in user's password and revokes sessions. | `{current_password, new_password}` -> `revoked_sessions`. |

## Users, profiles, and settings

| Method and path | What it does | Input -> response |
|---|---|---|
| `GET /users/me` | Reads the signed-in user's profile. | None -> profile, account status, privacy and notification settings. |
| `PATCH /users/me` | Updates profile and appearance fields. | Any of `{display_name, bio, profile_photo, theme, chat_accent, color_mode, liquid_glass, wallpaper}` -> updated fields. |
| `PATCH /users/me/preferences` | Saves client preferences. | JSON object with any subset of the keys listed below -> updated fields. |
| `PATCH /users/me/privacy` | Updates profile visibility and read-receipt privacy. | Any of `{last_seen, profile_photo, status, read_receipts}`. Visibility values: `everyone`, `contacts`, `nobody`. -> updated fields. |
| `PATCH /users/me/notifications` | Updates notification categories. | Any of `{messages, groups, calls, statuses, security}` -> updated fields. |
| `GET /users/me/sessions` | Lists active sign-in sessions. | None -> session IDs, device details, IP, creation and expiry times. |
| `DELETE /users/me/sessions/{session_id}` | Revokes one of the user's sessions. | None -> confirmation. |
| `POST /users/me/deactivate` | Deactivates the account and revokes its sessions. | `{password}` -> confirmation. |
| `GET /users/presence/{user_id}` | Reads a user's online and busy presence. | None -> `user_id`, `online`, `last_seen`, busy fields. |
| `GET /users/{username}` | Reads a limited public profile (sign-in required). | None -> ID, username, display name, photo, bio. |
| `GET /users/search/{query}` | Searches active users by name, username, or phone. | Path `query` (at least 2 characters) -> up to 20 profile matches, including `phone_match`. |
| `PATCH /users/me/premium-settings` | Updates premium-only features. | Any of `{verified_badge, force_read_receipts, live_typing, status_ads_enabled}` -> updated fields. |

Preference keys for `PATCH /users/me/preferences`:

- **Appearance and app:** `theme`, `chat_accent`, `color_mode`, `liquid_glass`, `wallpaper`, `font_size`, `language`, `show_fab`, `time_format`, `auto_download`, `sound`, `enter_is_send`, `low_data_calls`.
- **Notifications and messaging:** `msg_notif`, `group_notif`, `call_notif`, `status_like_notif`, `read_receipts`, `typing_indicator`, `previews`, `vibrate`.
- **Status and privacy:** `status_privacy`, `status_selected_contacts`, `status_excluded_contacts`, `status_validity`, `last_seen`, `profile_photo`, `about_privacy`, `groups_add`, `disappearing`.
- **Busy and Premium:** `busy_enabled`, `busy_message`, `busy_until`, `busy_scope`, `hide_live_typing`, `force_read_receipts`, `live_typing`, `status_ads_enabled`, `verified_badge`.

