## Realtime WebSocket

Connect to `wss://<your-backend>/api/v1/ws?token=<access_token>` (use `ws://` locally). The access token is required in the query string.

| Client packet | What it does | Server response |
|---|---|---|
| `{"t":"ping"}` | Keeps the connection and presence alive. | `{"t":"pong","ts":"..."}`. |
| `{"t":"send","c":"<conversation_id>","text":"Hello","ck":"<client_key>"}` | Sends a text message; `img`, `reply_to`, or `reply_to_message_id` can also be supplied. | `ack` packet with `ok`, message `id`, conversation `c`, and timestamp; failures include `err`. |
| `{"t":"rcpt","id":"<message_id>","c":"<conversation_id>","s":"delivered"}` | Reports delivery or read state (`s` is `delivered` or `read`). | Relays receipt updates to the sender. |
| `{"t":"typing","to":"<user_id>","typing":true,"draft":"..."}` | Sends typing/live-draft presence to a peer. | Peer receives a `typing` packet. |
| `{"t":"call","a":"offer","to":"<user_id>","callId":"...","sdp":"..."}` | Relays call signaling. Actions include `offer`, `answer`, `ice`, `ring`, and `hangup`; fields vary by action. | Peer receives a `call` packet; offline ring attempts return `unavailable`. |

The server also sends message, receipt, presence, typing, and call events over the open connection.